  "ingredients": [
    "3.5 pounds beef chuck roast (should be very well-marbled)",
    "3 tablespoons barbecue dry rub",
    "0.5 cup Kansas City style BBQ sauce",
    "4 sandwich or hoagie rolls",
    "1 (8 ounce) container cheese whiz, or sliced cheese as needed",
    "0.66 cup sautéed onions",
    "0.66 cup chopped jarred pickled peppers",
    "2 tablespoons sliced green onions"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients, and preheat the oven to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C). Season beef with dry rub, and double wrap in foil. Place on a sheet pan or in a baking dish, seam side up, and roast in the preheated oven for 2 1/2 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/uiXWag5O3TPJL7KOPKMuPwXqNd4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-8537970-kansas-city-style-burnt-ends-philly-cheesesteak-VAT-4x3-step-02-0209283744c34f51835817448701545e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8537970/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let rest for 1 hour. Unwrap and transfer to a cutting board. Reserve all juices. Cut into 1-inch cubes and transfer to a mixing bowl. Add cooking juices, more dry rub if desired, and bbq sauce. Mix well, wrap, and refrigerate overnight.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/s_QlI7v6QA9O7LQaGxv1Qg9V37k=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-8537970-kansas-city-style-burnt-ends-philly-cheesesteak-VAT-4x3-step-04-16c6374337b449a7a81eab783cb1899c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8537970/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C). Transfer beef into a shallow baking dish and brush generously with bbq sauce.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/9vbhEuzyF4onHNLPx_23kEISkO8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-8537970-kansas-city-style-burnt-ends-philly-cheesesteak-VAT-4x3-step-06-0072c7a83c884860acbea5ff69f85725.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8537970/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast in the preheated oven until meat starts to char around the edges, about 1 hour. Remove from oven and brush again with bbq sauce. Reduce oven temperature to 250 degrees F (120 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast until the \"burnt ends\" are as tender as you want, about 1 1/2 hours more.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/XMZo17QGuDQTU8taz8n9Gzvsq6A=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-8537970-kansas-city-style-burnt-ends-philly-cheesesteak-VAT-4x3-step-09-a-5692b7b0f9fc4d01ad9081d1dbb55879.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8537970/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer the \"burnt ends\" onto the rolls, and finish with cheese whiz, onions, peppers, and green onions.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Q7m709iwElqadZJLV6GZarrlUr4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-8537970-kansas-city-style-burnt-ends-philly-cheesesteak-VAT-4x3-step-09-b-cd63675f6ffa490d84df1345e0e4d2b4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8537970/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/6kziYUYw4Cl-JRTOyKXZ3dJc_3g=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-8537970-kansas-city-style-burnt-ends-philly-cheesesteak-VAT-hero-4x3-d9b81a9a6c624f7897b781302f4d0cd0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/8537970/step_07.webp"
    }
